{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Decomposition plan recorded in the description. Summary: completion.py (800) splits along its four call-graph clusters — the operation/orchestration stays in completion.py (~250 LOC, remains the stable __all__ seam via re-exports); the deterministic child-closure gate moves to NEW rebar/llm/completion_child_gate.py; verdict reconciliation + deterministic_child_failure move to NEW rebar/llm/completion_reconcile.py; the epic bug-screen DET layer (floor + candidate filter) moves HOME into epic_bug_screen.py (297 -> ~460), unifying the whole screen. completion_recovery.py (799) splits along its three clusters — criteria surface/bounds/coverage contract to NEW workflow/completion_criteria.py; exhaustion taxonomy + bounded diagnostics + failure finalization to NEW workflow/completion_failures.py; CompletionAgentStep orchestration stays (~420, keeps its documented __all__ via re-export). All moves behavior-preserving along existing seams; tests updated for import paths/monkeypatch targets only. String-swept monkeypatch sites already enumerated: test_ticket_description_limit.py:209/211/232 (stays valid via facade), test_eval_solver.py:203 (stays valid), test_completion_prefetch.py:120 and test_epic_bug_screen_4b54.py:230/450 (targets follow the moves)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786756147757887001,"uuid":"51f4c5b2-620f-40e4-9226-85577a4b9e15"}